ingredients:
  - "1/4 cup jowar"
  - "1/2 cup water (for pressure cooking)"
  - "1 tsp oil"
  - "1/4 tsp cumin"
  - "1/4 tsp mustard"
  - "1/2 tsp urad dal"
  - "1/2 pinch hing"
  - "1/2 small onion, sliced"
  - "1 1/2 green chilies, slit"
  - "1/2 tsp ginger, chopped (optional)"
  - "3/8 cup mixed veggies (beans, carrots, capsicum, methi leaves), chopped"
  - "Salt as needed"
instructions:
  - "Wash and soak jowar for at least 8 hours. Drain and add 1 cup water, then pressure cook for 2 whistles on medium flame and 1 more whistle on low flame."
  - "Once pressure settles, fluff up the cooked jowar."
  - "Heat oil in a pan, add cumin and mustard, allow them to crackle."
  - "Add urad dal and sauté until golden."
  - "Add chilies, onions, and ginger; sauté until onions turn soft."
  - "Add mixed veggies and sauté for 2 minutes."
  - "Cover and cook until soft. Sprinkle some water if needed."
  - "Add salt and turmeric, mix well."
  - "Add cooked jowar, mix well and sauté for 2 minutes."
  - "Stir in some lemon juice and garnish with coriander leaves. Serve warm."
